


# Security - Never commit sensitive files
.env
# WHY: `.env` alone does not cover a copy such as `.env.backup-2059` or
# `.env.2026-08-25`. A copy holds the same API token as the original, so the
# pattern below covers every suffix an operator adds while editing.
.env.*
!.env.example
!documentation/sample.env

# Copyrighted standard - do not redistribute (ASD-STE100 license restricts sharing)
# The distilled guide documentation/ASD-STE100_writing-guide.md is committed instead.
documentation/ASD-STE100_ISSUE9.pdf

# STE linter dictionary - generated locally from the licensed PDF, never committed
data/ste_dictionary.json

# Vendor reference corpus - do not redistribute (Juniper Networks copyright).
# Holds the Session Smart Networking documentation and the Juniper Mist PDFs that
# the NOC runbooks cite. The files are verbatim vendor text, so they follow the
# same rule as data/ste_dictionary.json above: generated locally, never committed.
# The distilled runbooks under documentation/noc-runbooks/ are committed instead.
# Rebuild the corpus with:
#   python scripts/fetch_ssr_docs.py
#   python scripts/pdf_to_markdown.py <downloaded.pdf>
documentation/references/

# Juniper hardening corpus - do not redistribute (Juniper Networks copyright).
# Issue #2754 staged 9,337 extracted PDF files and 4,006 converted Markdown files
# below the corpus root. The corpus root is the JUNIPER_CORPUS_ROOT setting, and
# it sits outside the worktree. The corpus measures 744 MB, so it never enters
# the repository. The distilled skill at .github/skills/hardening-junos/ is
# committed instead.
# Rebuild the corpus with:
#   python scripts/pdf_to_markdown.py <downloaded.pdf>
# The rules below guard against a corpus copy inside the worktree. git applies an
# ignore rule to an untracked path only. The one tracked PDF file therefore stays
# tracked.
juniper-doc-archives/
**/markdown/
**/extracted/
*.pdf

# A test fixture PDF is source, not a harvested artifact. Each one is under 4 KB
# and a test reads it at collection time. Without this rule the broad `*.pdf`
# rule above drops the fixture, and the test suite then fails on a fresh
# checkout with FileNotFoundError.
!tests/**/fixtures/*.pdf

.env.local
.env.production
.env.staging
*.log
# WHY: a saved test run is a local artifact, not source. `e2e-baseline.txt` was
# a pytest transcript that a `git add -A` swept into a commit twice.
e2e-baseline.txt
*-baseline.txt
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials.json
secrets.json
config.json

